  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Today I decided to update my own empty spectator avatar to be available as a fallback avatar, but this bug prevents me from doing so.\nAt some point in the past you could upload an empty avatar to Quest platform.\nMine was last updated on 12th of December 2020, which means this issue appeared after one of updates after that date.\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Ensure your project's target build is Android.\n2. On an new scene add an empty game object.\n3. Add an VRC_AvatarDescriptor to it. Nothing needs to be configured.\n4. Builder tab comes up empty and Unity console will get spammed with 2 similar errors as long as you have it open:\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1GzVy6ZzfoevnJ4KX9A4A_JFM37xFpGKQ/view?usp=sharing\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1ibjdzy2Ro9ipZKGIVW8ZxK2-fmHmbnNj/view?usp=sharing\nPutting a 2nd valid humanoid avatar with an animator in the scene with VRC_AvatarDescriptor properly doesn't seem to fix this issue either.\nThis bug does not happen if you have the same empty avatar with project set for PC platform. Some screenshots attached.",
